  "prs": {
    "gunnchos-sitePR18": {
      "url": "https://github.com/gunnchOS3k/gunnchos-site/pull/18",
      "state": "open",
      "merged": false,
      "draft": false,
      "base": "main",
      "base_sha": "acd021361c4c3312dd49ebfbe29238f221b6434e",
      "head": "v1/passport-pass2u-event-final",
      "head_sha": "3de66816db4be9f8261961cfe8b52659237c8f37",
      "merge_commit_sha": null,
      "body": "Preserve the approved Passport constellation and dark foundation while integrating pink sampled from the owner logo, a compact controller/wordmark lockup, and exact source-pixel 3K/MLV marks. The profile hero, event card, print view, and social preview share the branding; QR modules remain dark-on-white.\n\nAdd a local `passport:pass2u -- --profile <opaque-id>` export for existing opted-in profiles. The complete owner kit includes a ZIP, front design reference, clean background/strip, small logos/thumbnail, QR PNG/SVG, field JSON, concise iPhone guide, and a 1080×1920 Photos fallback. Owner signatures are omitted for other participant profiles. No Pass2U account/API calls, signing, payment, or automatic publication occur. Remove the dormant official Apple action from the event card; this event path needs no Apple Developer enrollment.\n\nValidation: 35 focused Passport unit tests and 10 desktop/mobile browser checks pass, including independent decoding of exported QR and fallback, exact handwriting source pixels, share/privacy/lenses, pink focus, print controls, accessibility, and mobile width. Native lint/Next build and secret/registry checks pass. Required Cloudflare runtime checks follow before exact-main deployment. Existing CI remains intact.\n\nAn optional broad `tsc --noEmit` check reports the same four preexisting errors on unchanged main (Playwright/Axe type mismatch and absent React DOM declarations); no suppressions or unrelated type changes are introduced. Physical iPhone Pass2U installation, camera scanning, and event acceptance remain owner-only. V1_PASSPORT_HUMAN_PASS remains false.\n\nThe existing Passport authorization permits a normal focused merge and deployment to gunnchos-site after green CI/runtime checks. Wrangler, DNS, authentication, public registry content, and unrelated products remain unchanged.\n"
    },
    "gunnchos-sitePR19": {
      "url": "https://github.com/gunnchOS3k/gunnchos-site/pull/19",
      "state": "closed",
      "merged": true,
      "draft": false,
      "base": "main",
      "base_sha": "acd021361c4c3312dd49ebfbe29238f221b6434e",
      "head": "v1/site-brand-taste-pass",
      "head_sha": "42ced4bc427cdbddead7b3e67aa8ef6c67b23574",
      "merge_commit_sha": "3a46b0eb74eab7e41a4960fd5f6621c9d1c7170e",
      "body": "## Result\n\nConverges the public website on the owner-approved PR #19 taste direction: navy/cyan/pink with restrained constellation cues, clear routes for learning, research, devices, play, projects, and community, and responsive page hierarchy. Existing truth boundaries and the Passport visual/behavior surface are preserved.\n\nThe final closure changes the workspace label to **My Home**, makes owner-verified **hello@gunnchos.com** the active public contact channel, removes the obsolete mailbox disclaimer, and completes unique search metadata, production canonicals, OG/Twitter metadata, grounded Organization/WebSite and nested breadcrumb JSON-LD, deterministic sitemap, production robots, and preview noindex protection.\n\nThe owner explicitly authorized the full **278×252 JPEG** as the V1 canonical-source exception. The public header preserves its entire artwork without a circular crop; opaque icon derivatives only downscale; the 1200×630 social card uses the approved visual system with the JPEG at native size. No upscaling, AI redraw, reconstruction, fabricated transparency, or destructive cropping. A higher-resolution transparent logo is a **non-blocking future asset-quality improvement**.\n\n## Validation and production verification\n\nTypecheck, lint (two existing warnings), focused SEO unit tests, secret scan, Cloudflare configuration, and both Next/OpenNext builds passed. Focused local browser checks: 15 passes / three intentional skips. [CI on final head](https://github.com/gunnchOS3k/gunnchos-site/actions/runs/37557120344) passed: 74 unit tests / one opt-in remote skip; 70 browser tests / 12 intentional skips.\n\nMarked ready and merged normally. Final PR head: `42ced4bc427cdbddead7b3e67aa8ef6c67b23574`. Merge and exact deployed main: `3a46b0eb74eab7e41a4960fd5f6621c9d1c7170e`. A clean detached checkout was built with that SHA and the accepted branded URLs; its source tree is identical to the green PR head. Existing `gunnchos-site` Worker version: `d6da71fd-ee12-45c7-a8db-d4f4364312ca`, active at 100%.\n\n[Production](https://gunnchos.com) verification passed across 15 landing pages and six 390px/320px layout checks. Homepage, Contact, My Home, Research, Devices, Play, Campus/WAIKE, Gallery, Status, unique titles/descriptions, production canonicals, OG/Twitter metadata, icon/social asset delivery, Organization/WebSite/Breadcrumb JSON-LD, deterministic sitemap, robots, and deployed Status SHA passed. The canonical public JPEG is byte-identical to the supplied original. Contact presents `hello@gunnchos.com` as the active public mailto channel and the obsolete disclaimer is gone.\n\nProduction remains indexable. The fallback workers.dev host and [new version preview](https://d6da71fd-gunnchos-site.gunnchos-finds.workers.dev) have noindex protection. The unchanged focused Passport suite passed all eight production checks, including lenses/event card, QR decoding, share fallback, closed Wallet, vCard privacy, mobile layout/focus, and accessibility. All five existing Open Lab fail-closed checks passed.\n\n`V1_SITE_HUMAN_TASTE_PASS=true` is recorded after successful production verification based on explicit owner approval. No other gate is inferred. DNS was unchanged. RC2/V1 remains unpublished. Passport, Anime Aggressors, Archive of Life, and other product engineering remain paused.\n\nAsset provenance: `public/brand/provenance.json`; source notes: `docs/BRAND_ASSETS.md`; owner-only [search-engine checklist](https://github.com/gunnchOS3k/gunnchos-site/blob/main/docs/SEO_LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md). The local post-deployment report, full verification JSON, screenshots, build/deploy logs, and Passport results are saved under `artifacts/production-closure` in the exact-main deployment checkout. Historical pre-production review artifacts retain their original source/version and gate state.\n"
    },
    "gunnchos-waike-learning-platformPR27": {
      "url": "https://github.com/gunnchOS3k/gunnchos-waike-learning-platform/pull/27",
      "state": "closed",
      "merged": true,
      "draft": false,
      "base": "main",
      "base_sha": "90fb9c5ceab51d99dfff7b5e6d1775fd1dca85d6",
      "head": "v1/full-learner-journey",
      "head_sha": "c73fae5945338d28c9915024c468fc0925027e93",
      "merge_commit_sha": "2641042936f3b965daccb11091c80cbc6fa64f91",
      "body": "The public learner path now opens authored content from all 18 verified curriculum packages without requiring a school Hub. Learners can browse lessons, assignment instructions, quizzes, labs, and portfolio instructions while school schedules, submissions, grades, messages, and AI remain explicitly unavailable until a real Hub supplies them.\n\nDigital Confidence now packages the material already authored in the pinned canonical curriculum, including its shared GENERAL_IT lessons, quizzes, labs, rubrics, outcomes, AI policy, and offline pack. The compiler respects the explicit WAIKE_ROOT pin. Native pack tests use isolated compile outputs and preserve all trust/tamper/role assertions.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Exact curriculum pin: 63ba9f25ac6b8d8d1b6dd118923566fd51c57b62; 18/18 packages compile and verify.\n- Full make test: 126 core, 99 Gate A, 201 Gate B, 74 Gate C, 16 Gate D, 38 Rust, 78 frontend passed.\n- Final frontend regression: 96 tests passed, including all 18 content routes; lint passed.\n- make build passed for the pack, Vite production bundle, and native Rust binary.\n- Final Gate C/D verifiers honor WAIKE_ALLOW_FAKE_AI=0; production AI acceptance remains false.\n- Public curriculum validator and signed-payload reachability evidence passed.\n\nDetailed package IDs/hashes, real-content matrix, and test evidence are in reports/V1_PUBLIC_LEARNER_JOURNEY.md and .json.\n\nOwner review is requested. V1_WAIKE_HUMAN_PASS, production school-Hub/hosted acceptance, Pixel/device acceptance, external OneRoster/QTI/LTI certification, production signing/notarization, and independent security/accessibility/privacy certification remain false/open. This PR does not deploy or authorize an automatic merge.\n"
    },
    "pedestrian-pursuitPR41": {
