      "base_sha": "a10cfe7535cde6508699735930378a2801fa31f4",
      "head": "world/spatial-commons-neighborhood-v1",
      "head_sha": "bf08de4caeea3d2a80ce79233c906e19ae7f96a5",
      "merge_commit_sha": "2c14f13fcb049cb1ea71c9f4900c0abdbc37cd6d",
      "body": "## Summary\n- Replaces the signed-in flat home block with a room-to-room neighborhood on the existing React Three Fiber stack: 3k MLV Commons, a player house (exterior plus front room and study), and a campus transit plaza.\n- All seven destinations are physically present and named Gary, Ghana, Guyana, Geelong, Ruhr, Gaza, and Graham Land. Each has an enterable exterior, lobby, learning room, and gallery. Geometry is original and stylized.\n- Affiliation claims stay false. Gaza has no coordinates and no site claim. Ruhr is the world label for the existing Germany catalog slug. This does not flip HUMAN_7GC_* or other LIVE gates, and it does not replace the schematic drawings on PR #6.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `node --test tests/world/spatial_neighborhood.test.mjs tests/privacy/*.test.mjs tests/deployment/portal_return.test.mjs`\n- [x] `tsc --noEmit` in `apps/mlv-web`\n- [x] Local walk: Commons → house exterior → front room → study → Commons → transit (seven names visible) → Gary exterior → Gary lobby → Gary gallery\n- [x] Same enterable stack walked for Ghana, Guyana, Geelong, Ruhr, Gaza, and Graham Land\n- [ ] Not deployed. Screenshots are local development captures in `artifacts/world/spatial_commons/`\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)"
